# Code owners for StudCraft.
#
# Listing an owner here assigns them as a reviewer automatically. It does not
# yet *require* their approval: `main` currently requires 0 approving reviews,
# because there is one maintainer and GitHub does not allow approving your own
# pull request. Raising that to 1 today would make every PR unmergeable,
# `enforce_admins` being on.
#
# On the day a second maintainer joins, both of these change together:
#   1. add them below,
#   2. set required_approving_review_count to 1 and enable
#      require_code_owner_reviews on the `main` branch protection.
#
# Until then this file does the useful half — routing review requests — without
# the half that would deadlock.

# Everything, by default.
*                       @jujorie

# The ruleset itself. Changes here need someone who knows the design code.
/docs/                  @jujorie

# Process and design constitution.
/system/                @jujorie
/CODE_OF_DESIGN.md      @jujorie
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @jujorie
/AGENTS.md              @jujorie

# CI gates and the release/archive automation. Breaking these silently breaks
# every other guarantee in the repo.
/.github/               @jujorie
/scripts/               @jujorie

# Spec deltas and archived changes.
/openspec/              @jujorie
